  "rationale": "**Verdict:** `requirements.cli.setup_css` is implemented, marked, and tested. I found no gaps.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/setup.rs`, `run` (the `{impl}` marker is at line 126), covers each obligation:\n  - **Missing `additional-css`:** a new array containing only the Habeas stylesheet path is created.\n  - **Existing array:** entries are left in place. The Habeas path, computed by `css_relative`, is pushed only if no existing entry already equals it. This gives \"preserve existing entries\" and \"at most once\", including on re-runs.\n  - **Not an array:** it returns `output.html.additional-css must be an array`. This happens before any file or `Cargo.toml` change, because the book is only edited in memory until the final write.\n- `css_relative` (`src/setup.rs`, line 11) is marked `{impl}`. It builds the `<src>/habeas.css` path used for the entry.\n- `is_configured` only reads the stylesheet entry to report whether setup is complete. It does not add or change anything, so a `{cite}` there is appropriate. It is not unmarked implementation.\n- I found no behavior in the marked code that goes beyond this requirement or another one it implements.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/setup.rs`, `setup_is_repeatable` (`{test}` marker at line 77):\n  - The fixture's `book.toml` starts with `additional-css = [\"md/custom.css\"]`.\n  - Setup runs twice.\n  - The test asserts that `md/custom.css` is preserved, `md/habeas.css` is present, and `md/habeas.css` appears exactly once.\n- `setup_rejects_invalid_book_configuration` (`{test}` marker at line 144) covers the error case. A string-valued `additional-css = \"wrong\"` makes setup fail with the expected stderr message.\n- Missing `additional-css` is exercised by `setup_uses_src_when_book_table_or_source_setting_is_absent`, though that test does not carry a `{test}` marker for this requirement. Only the first two tests are marked for `setup_css`. The behavior is simple, so this is a minor omission.\n\n**Minor observation:** the toml_edit indexing could panic if `output` or `output.html` is a non-table value. This is outside what the requirement specifies.",
